 ### Nearest particle calculation technique
-A technique applied to multiple volumes to resolve the depth-direction artifact of the SPT algorithm by accurately determining particle positions along the ray [S2, abstract only]. It constructs a cumulative distribution function (CDF) of the particle spacing and develops a technique for calculating the nearest particle along the interval using the CDF [S2, abstract only].
+A technique applied to multiple volumes to resolve the depth-direction artifact of the SPT algorithm by accurately determining particle positions along the ray [S2, abstract only]. It sets itself apart from the basic SPT method by replacing the fixed pre-defined depth assumption with a cumulative distribution function (CDF) of particle spacing to locate the nearest particle along the interval [S2, abstract only]. Choose this variant when rendering multiple irregular volumes to eliminate depth-direction artifacts [S2, abstract only]. See [Nearest particle calculation technique](link-to-child-article-if-exists).
 
